Shared `_resolution_candidate` retains descending local revision order and exhaustive latest-state inspection. It remembers only the first active/revoked/superseded candidate but continues through all records: a missing older state still raises its native AttributeError. Streaming `.only(id,case_id,component,revision).iterator(chunk_size=100)` avoids eagerly hydrating unselected LOCAL configuration envelopes or retaining the queryset result cache. It does not bound total database work/driver memory, add a history cap, guarantee consistent READ COMMITTED observation, or eliminate the later selected and inherited-source envelope loads.

Resolve still captures at before selection, performs the selected latest-state read again, retains revoked/no-fallback behavior, calls application_health before expected_revision/native validation, and preserves exact result/reason/time outcomes. It never substitutes the supplied case instance for selected.case. The downstream AST from the second state read is unchanged against8aaaecc and covered by a pure digest assertion.

Four pure checks pass normal/-O: exhaustive scalar stream, malformed missing-state failure after a winner, no-eligible/superseded selection, unchanged downstream AST. Six native test definitions cover missing draft/validated, newest revoked over superseded, large unselected draft envelopes, actual selected second-state SQL observation, expected-revision/time outcomes, and genuine inherited scope source/revocation/fresh selected.case. They are UNRUN; DB-forbidden discovery/static/model checks only. Malformed state-less history is tested only in pure selection logic, never forged into PostgreSQL or bypassing native guards. Huge unvalidated drafts use permitted save_draft; they are never activated as policy.

